\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 86r-97r {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Antonius Haneron}}\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1 : De epistolis brevibus edendis
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Anthonii Haneron oratoris famosissimi Lauoniensis studii doctoris compendium de breuibus epistulis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ...\u8249 \'8b Darunter Nota (nachgetragen): \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Hoc compendium rethorice famosus studii Wiennensis magister Georgius de Peurbach compilauit. Et sub alieno nomine ut hic scriptum est ex humilitate intitulavit anno Christi 1458. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  (86r) Prolog: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Si male vtile erit praeceptor optime quod tantopere me facere cogis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash  (85r-97r) Text: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Parcium epistole legittime \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (! vielm.: latine) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 quaedam extrinsice sunt ac accidentales \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ut data. Fac bene valeas. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  Kolophon: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Anthonii Haneron oratoris mirifici \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 compendium de breuibus epistolis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 feliciter explicit per Paulum Hebemkrieg baccalaureum Wiennensem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 in vincula sancti Petri lviii \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 [1458 August 1]\u8249 \'8b
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Von der Nachtragshand Georg von Peuerbach zugeschrieben. \endash  Druck: GW 12127. \endash  Lit.: \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20\cf1 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 VL 3 (1981), Sp. 434 (Jozef Ijsewijn). \endash  Emil J. Polak, Medieval and Renaissance Letter Treatises and Form Letters. A census of Manuscripts Found in Albania, Austria, Bulgaria, France, Germany, and Italy. Leiden/Boston 2015, S. 486.}

