\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (309ra)\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Tractatulus de arte moriendi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b Nachtrag von Hand Schwerzenbecks: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 magistri Nycolai de Dinklsp\u252 \'fchhl\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \endash  Prolog: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Incipit prohemium de arte moriendi in nomine sancte et indiuidue Trinitatis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \endash  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Cum de presentis exilij miseria\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ...  \u8249 \'8b \endash  (309ra) Text: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Prima particula de laude mortis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ...\u8249 \'8b \endash  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Cum omnium terribilium mors\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ...\u8249 \'8b \endash  ... (316va)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  In tuo conspectu gaudeat in eternum. Qui cum Patre\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ... etc.  \endash    \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Cum autem tota salus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ... \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 mori distat. Explicit tractatulus de arte moriendi perutilis cuilibet christiano uolenti secure ab hoc seculo migrare anno li\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 mo\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  per \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 [...]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (Hebr\u228 \'e4ische Buchstaben? In Bleistift eingetragen: TIA U? )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  Vdalricum etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b
