\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 145r-166v  {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezper[0].4100/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Johannes Hagen de Indagine}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 : {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\chcbpat17\cf1 Soliloquium hominis devoti}}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Incipit soliloquium hominis deuoto suos defectus cognoscentis ac nouissima prouidentis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b  Nachtrag von Hand Schwerzenbecks: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 compositum per venerabilem virum Johannem de Indagnie \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  priorem ordinis Carthusiensis in Erfordia. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Uerbum michi est ad te, o princeps regum terre ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 finem valeam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 iocunde te duce pervenire qui cum Patre et Filio ... Amen. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Explicit soliloquium compositum per venerabilem patrem Johannem de Indagine priorem ordinis Carthusiensis  conuentus in Erfordia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \endash    167rv leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Lit.: Joseph Klapper, Der Erfurter Kart\u228 \'e4user Johannes Hagen: ein Reformtheologe des 15. Jahrhunderts, Bd. 2, Leipzig, 1961,  S. 21 (D 20, Nr. 10); Stephen M. Metzger, The Manuscripts of Writings by Ioannes Hagen de Indagine, O. Cart., in: Bulletin de philosophie m\u233 \'e9di\u233 \'e9vale 50 (2008), S. 175\endash 256 (Hs. genannt  S. 211-212); \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs20 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 VL Bd. 3, Sp. 393 (Dieter Mertens), Hs. genannt. \endash  Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung, u.a., Clm. 18606.}

