\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (145v) \u220 \'dcberschrift: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Gloza hec\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 infra super mysticam theologiam beati Dyonisii excerpta est per venerabilem Johannem Schlippacher ex duobus commentis scilicet Linconiensis et Johannis Sarraceni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \endash   \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Prologus Johannis Sarraceni ad Odonem sancti Dionisii abbatem in librum de mistica theologia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ante misticam theologiam simbolica theologia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ...  \endash   \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Prefacio glose sequentis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Mistice theologie beati Dionisij tres habuntur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ... \endash  (146r)  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Incipit liber sancti Dionisij cum glosa eiusdem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b\plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Trinitas\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 scilicet diuinarum personarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1  ...  \endash  (155r) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Hec Linconiensis in fine sui commenti\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \endash  \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Ex binis commentis bis binisque diebus / hec humilis glosula colligitur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 1477\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 . \endash  155v leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\tx4605\ql\ri0\sb0\sa195\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20 Druck (ohne Glosse):  Dionysiaca I, 565-602. Parallel\u252 \'fcberlieferung: Melk, Benediktinerstift, Cod. 1560 (61, B 26), f. 3r-12v; Wien \u214 \'d6NB, Cod. 790, 128ra-132ra.}

