\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Incipiunt omelie beati Augustini episcopi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b Ad lectorem: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 In cuiuscumque manus libellus iste venerit rogo et cum grandi humilitate supplico \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash  Prolog: \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Prologus primus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Pro intuitu paterne pietatis et qualiscumque pastoris sollicitudine \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 (2rb) Index sermonum. \endash  (3ra) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Omelia prima ante diem natalis domini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Propicia diuinitate fratres dilectissimi iam prope est dies ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  (5ra) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Omelia 2\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 a\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Satis habundeque dixisse me credo ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \endash  (6ra) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Omelia 3\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24\cf1 a \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ante natalem domini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Omnes scripture quas nunc audiuimus fratres karissimi leticiam publicam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash  ... (83va) \u8250 \'9b\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Sermo beati Augustini\plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 \u8249 \'8b \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs24\cf1 Quando celebramus diem fratrum defunctorum in mente habere debemus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs24\cf1 ... \endash  85r leer.
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa240\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs20\cf1 Sammlung von 67 Sermones, u.a. aus Augustinus, Sermones ad populum (PL 39). \endash  Die Prologe aus Caesarius Arelatensis, Sermo 2, CC 103, S. 18-19, der erste Sermo ebenfalls Caesarius Arelatensis, Sermo 187, CC 104, S. 763-766. Der letzte Sermo Augustinus, Sermo 197, CC 41b, S. 494-499.}

